<title>UK: Barclays jumps to fresh record peak.</title>
<headline>Barclays jumps to fresh record peak.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Barclays jumped by almost seven percent to a fresh record peak amid renewed hopes for another share buyback, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 0957 GMT, the shares were up 10-1/2p to 1021-1/2p. They rose as high as 1026p earlier. </p>
<p>Barclays has said it intends to buy back more of its shares.</p>
<p>An announcement today by the National Australia Bank that it planned a stock repurchase &quot;brings the share buyback story back into play,&quot; said one market maker.</p>
<p>-- Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
